# WhatsApp reservation confirmation — delivery contract

A reservation confirmation is the voucher image + its text, sent to the
**guest**, then copied to the **Booking Team group**
(`readWaConfig().teamChatId`, `...@g.us`, posted from the group line
`rockyjio`). Any change that touches this path must keep every rule below.

## 1. Order — guest first, group second

1. Guest voucher image, then the guest voucher text (one line, sticky per
   guest — `glLineFor_` / `glRemember_`).
2. Booking Team group copy (`tplGroupCopy_`), image then text.
3. Policy cards (`policyQueueBehind_`) behind the guest voucher. They are not
   part of the confirmation and never delay steps 1–2.

The group copy is released only after the guest voucher is **delivered**, or
when the guest deadline in §3 expires. It must never go out ahead of the
guest. (2 Oct 2026, RDEC10726 and RDEC10826: the group copies went out at
2:04 PM and the guests' at 2:14–2:16 PM.)

## 2. "Delivered" means sent, not queued

- Delivered means Evolution accepted the send. In the Send Queue tab that is
  `Status = sent`. `{ ok:true, queued:true }` from `sendTpl` only means
  "written to the queue".
- `sheet_sync_outbox.status = done` only means Apps Script answered. Never
  show "sent" in the app, or skip a fallback, because of it.
- The app shows queued → sent / failed for the guest and the group
  separately, from the Send Queue state for that booking ID.

## 3. Fallback within 2 minutes (T = the moment staff tap send)

| By | Must be true |
|---|---|
| T + 60 s | Guest voucher sent. If not, move it once to the next live line (`paceMoveOffDeadLine_` / `paceLiveLine_`), and move the guest's whole remaining thread with it. |
| T + 120 s | Guest voucher sent, **or** marked `failed` and the desk alerted with the booking ID. |
| T + 120 s | Group copy sent. If the guest is still not delivered, send the group copy anyway with a line saying guest delivery is pending/failed, so the desk can act. |

- Voucher rows (`why` starts `voucher <ID>` / `voucher copy <ID>`) jump
  ahead of every other row in `paceQueueSweep`. Policy cards, fliers,
  Justdial and similar rows may wait. Pacing gaps (30 s per guest, 15 s per
  line, ±5 s jitter) must still fit inside the 2 minutes.
- Delivery must never depend on the 1-minute time trigger alone. A voucher
  enqueued when its clocks allow is sent inline at enqueue. A watchdog
  outside Apps Script (Supabase) drains any voucher row that is more than
  60 s overdue. A stalled trigger is an incident, not a delay. (2 Oct 2026:
  RDEC10926's rows were due at 2:19 PM and were still queued at 2:30 PM.
  Earlier vouchers arrived 40–70 minutes late, all in one burst.)
- A fallback **moves** the existing row (new line, new due time, note
  `moved off X to Y`). It never appends a second row for the same message.

## 4. No duplication — one message per key

Idempotency key: `bookingId | recipient (guest digits or group JID) | part`,
where `part` ∈ `voucher-image`, `voucher-text`, `group-image`, `group-text`,
`policy-1..3`.

- Before enqueueing, retrying or falling back, look the key up (Send Queue /
  delivery ledger):
  - `sent` → skip it.
  - `queued` → do not add another row. Expedite the existing one.
  - `failed` → re-send on the same row.
- A re-tap of **Send Voucher on WhatsApp**, Save/Share, or the
  booking-saved auto-send resends only the parts not yet `sent`. A full
  second copy needs an explicit "send again" confirmation from staff.
  (2 Oct 2026: re-taps added rows 3386–3389 for RDEC10926. The guest had
  extra copies queued from both Receptionist and rockyjio.)
- The guest hears from one number end to end. A fallback moves the thread;
  it never sends the same part from a second line.
- Supabase `sheet-sync` never re-forwards a WhatsApp action
  (`sendTpl`, `guestMsg`, `sendDoc`, re-share) once Apps Script has
  answered. Retry only when the request failed before reaching Apps Script.
  Any other retry is a duplicate.

## 5. Action names must exist on both sides

- Every action the app dispatches for WhatsApp must have a handler in
  `doPost` in the live Apps Script. The re-share button currently dispatches
  `welcomeShare`, which Apps Script rejects with `Unknown action:
  welcomeShare`, so the re-share never sends anything. Rename it to a
  handled action, or add the handler, in the same release.
- `sheet-sync` marks `Unknown action` as a permanent failure and surfaces
  it. It does not retry it up to 12 times.

## 6. Checklist for any change to this path

- [ ] A new booking: the guest voucher is `sent` before the group copy, and
      both are `sent` within 2 minutes (check `?action=sendQueue&by=Rakesh`).
- [ ] Guest line down: the voucher moves to the next live line once, and the
      group still gets its copy within 2 minutes.
- [ ] Sweep trigger disabled: the voucher still goes within 2 minutes, via the
      inline send or the watchdog.
- [ ] Tapping Send Voucher twice adds no new Send Queue rows for parts already
      queued or sent.
- [ ] The re-share action reaches a real handler (no `Unknown action` in
      `sheet_sync_outbox.last_error`).
